                                <h1 id=3D"ios-and-macos-installation-and-se=
tup">iOS and macOS Installation and Setup</h1>
<h2 id=3D"prerequisites">Prerequisites<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"h=
ttps://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/iOS.html#prerequisit=
es" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1=
em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>
<p>A supported environment. See <strong><a href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.o=
rg/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/prerequisites.html">Installation Prerequisi=
tes</a></strong></p>
<h2 id=3D"setting-up-cocos2d-x">Setting up Cocos2d-x<a class=3D"anchorjs-li=
nk " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/iOS.ht=
ml#setting-up-cocos2d-x" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=
=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h=
2>
<p>You can get started with <strong>Cocos2d-x</strong> by either downloadin=
g a self-contained
<strong>.zip</strong> from the <a href=3D"https://cocos2d-x.org/download" t=
arget=3D"_blank">website</a> or by cloning our
<a href=3D"https://github.com/cocos2d/cocos2d-x" target=3D"_blank">GitHub R=
epo</a>. Pick what works for you.
<strong>There is no need to do both.</strong></p>
<h3 id=3D"by-downloading-a-zip-archive">By downloading a .zip archive<a cla=
ss=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/in=
stallation/iOS.html#by-downloading-a-zip-archive" aria-label=3D"Anchor" dat=
a-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; paddin=
g-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>
<p>Download Cocos2d-x and unzip it. (maybe: <strong>~/</strong> or <strong>=
~/Projects</strong> )</p>
<p>  <img src=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/iO=
S-img/unzip.png" alt=3D""></p>
<p>  <img src=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/iO=
S-img/unzipping.png" alt=3D""></p>
<h3 id=3D"cloning-from-github">Cloning from GitHub<a class=3D"anchorjs-link=
 " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/iOS.html=
#cloning-from-github" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B=
" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>
<p>Use the following commands to clone our GitHub repo and get your environ=
ment setup.
If you are not familar with GitHub's workflow, <a href=3D"https://guides.gi=
thub.com/activities/hello-world/" target=3D"_blank">learn it</a> or downloa=
d
using the step above, <strong>By downloading a .zip archive</strong>.</p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> &lt;to=
 <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">where</span> you want to <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">clone</span> this repo&gt;

git <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">clone</span> git@github.com:cocos2d/cocos=
2d-x.git

git submodule update --init

git submodule update

./download-deps.py
</code></pre>
<h2 id=3D"make-sure-you-have-a-working-environment">Make sure you have a wo=
rking environment!<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-=
x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/iOS.html#make-sure-you-have-a-working-en=
vironment" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"=
font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>
<p>See <strong>Prerequisites</strong> above. This means a working <strong>P=
ython</strong>, having run <strong><cocos2d-x root=3D"">/setup.py&gt;</coco=
s2d-x></strong>,
updated your <strong>$PATH</strong> and run <strong>source ~/.bash_profile<=
/strong>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"build-and-run">Build and Run<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"h=
ttps://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/iOS.html#build-and-r=
un" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1=
em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>
<p><strong>Use cmake</strong></p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-bash"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> COCO=
S2DX/tests/cpp-tests
mkdir ios-build
<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> ios-build
cmake ..
make
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Use Xcode</strong></p>
<p>First use CMake to generate Xcode project,</p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-bash"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> COCO=
S2DX/tests/cpp-tests
mkdir ios-build
<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> ios-build
cmake .. -GXcode -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=3DiOS
</code></pre>
<p>then open <code>cpp-tests.xcodeproj</code> and select <code>cpp-tests</c=
ode> to run.</p>
<p><strong>Use cocos command line tools</strong></p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-bash"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> COCO=
S2DX/tests/cpp-tests
cocos run -p ios
</code></pre>
